WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.501
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:06.067
who stars on "This Is Us,"

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:08.567
which airs Tuesdays at
9:00 p.m. on NBC.

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:11.234
Everyone please welcome
Milo Ventimiglia!

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:13.334
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:16.267
Come on!
That's my man right there.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:17.367
-What's going on?
What's going on?

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:18.367
What's going on?

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.133
-It's so great
to see you, buddy.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:22.100
Happy, happy New Year to you.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.734
-Happy New Year to you, as well.
Sorry I'm not around.

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.300
I was hoping to be
in New York with you,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.367
but production and protocols
and all that, so...

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.000
-Next time.
Congrats on the premiere.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.167
A good man.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:33.667
I want to talk to you about
a couple things.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.434
You know I follow you
on Instagram,

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:38.400
and it's a
very interesting follow.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.567
It's a good follow.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:42.067
I like it because --
-Because it's nothing.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:43.667
-Yes, that's correct.

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:46.467
It is nothing,
and then it's something.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.367
It's like, all of a sudden --

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:51.033
You post like every couple
months or a month or so.

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:54.601
You'll post like
100 photos at once.

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:57.067
-Yeah. Like, I've realized
sometimes, it's kind of like,

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.501
"Wow, I really haven't been
on in a while,

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.300
and I've been living life
and I've been hiking

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.934
and I've been seeing
people and friends

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:04.434
and family and all that."

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:07.200
And I kind of have
this collection of photos

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.534
in a folder on my phone
that I've just kind of,

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:13.334
you know,
taken over a period of time,

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:15.100
like six months,
and then I'm like,

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.133
"Alright, let me
just put up 100.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.734
Why not?"
-Yeah, they really are.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.200
They're like --
Yeah, 100 photos.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.234
And you just look through them,

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:22.267
and everyone's like,
"Oh, my gosh."

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:23.567
And then they go everywhere.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:26.267
And they're --
Some are beautiful.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:27.801
Some are just cool.

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:29.067
Some --
-Some are ridiculous.

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:30.400
-Yes.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.367
-Like, I've had some --
Like, there was one -- It was --

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:38.033
I took a photo of my couch
in my trailer.

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:39.534
And just the way the light
was hitting it

00:01:39.534 --> 00:01:40.667
and the lines,
and it kind of lined up.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:41.834
And people were like,

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.701
"Is this a couch that is
on your Instagram now?

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:45.801
Are we supposed to like that?"

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:48.667
-Yeah.
Pictures of couches. Why not?

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:49.801
-Yeah, sure, why not?

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:52.200
-I started getting my
photos printed out

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.667
because I miss
holding the photos

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.801
and putting them in albums
and looking at them

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.234
and having people go,
"Oh, yeah,"

00:01:58.234 --> 00:01:59.701
and all these, man, 'cause
everything is just on my phone.

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:04.234
I'm going to get a photo that
you posted printed out, too.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.801
Is this a picture of your --
Is this just your gym shorts

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:08.033
or what are these?

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.000
-Yeah. Those are my shorts.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.033
Ride 'em high, kids.
-Yeah, ride 'em high, kids.

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.601
I think -- It made me laugh when
you said "Ride 'em high,"

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:19.000
because it came from some
paparazzi photo I saw of you,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.400
I guess, leaving the gym?

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.667
Is that what it was?

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.467
-I was leaving the gym,
funny enough,

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:26.734
post-appearing on your show.

00:02:26.734 --> 00:02:27.934
-Is that right?

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:29.968
You appeared on our show,
and it got you pumped up,

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:32.033
ready to go work out?

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.267
-I was so excited.
I was so charged up.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:36.834
It was like "Scarface."
I was ready to go.

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:39.701
I had the best leg day
of my life, and there it is.

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:41.968
-Yeah, and, so, you work out
and you have a good workout,

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:44.701
and then you come out,
and "Ride 'em high, kids."

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:46.601
This is what's in the --
-Ride 'em high, kids.

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:47.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah!

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:48.834
-Oh, man.

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:53.601
That was so much --
I really had no idea.

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:55.534
So, when I work out, you know,

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:57.167
I'm with my trainer,
Jason Walsh,

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:58.868
and we're just, you know,
kind of meatheads

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:00.834
throwing around a lot of weight.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:03.667
And when I work out,
I kind of pull my shorts up.

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:04.701
-Yeah.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.167
-And so then,
when I left the gym

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:09.567
and the photograph got taken,
and then it went bananas --

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:11.501
-It really did.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:15.968
-It went crazy. Literally crazy.
Like broke-the-Internet crazy.

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:18.000
And I was -- They were like,
"Oh, my God.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.234
Milo wears short shorts.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:20.434
It's the summer of
short shorts."

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:22.133
There's "New York Times"
articles.

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:23.501
There's "GQ" articles.

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:25.400
There's all these articles about
Milo and his short shorts.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.400
Yeah, seriously.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.601
And I'm just like,

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:29.200
"Guys, they were actually
really normal length.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.033
I just have,
like, kind of meaty thighs,

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:33.300
and I pulled them up and I
walked out and they stuck."

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.634
-Yeah. You yanked them up, man.

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:36.567
You've got some
muscular legs there.

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:37.834
You had a good workout.
It was a leg day, I guess.

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:39.167
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.000
-Every day is a good leg day.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.434
-Not only is "This Is Us" back,
but next month,

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:45.667
we're going to see you
in the new season of

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.934
"The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel."

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:50.667
-Yes, you are.
-That is -- Reunited.

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:52.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:55.434
Reunited with
Amy Sherman-Palladino.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:59.067
-Yeah. It's, you know,
back in -- It's amazing.

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:04.300
I mean, you know, Amy and
Dan Palladino, her husband,

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:08.100
who also is an incredibly
accomplished writer, you know,

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.601
they really gave me my break.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:12.734
Like, they were the ones that
kind of put me on the map

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:15.167
with "Gilmore" and with Jess,
your favorite, I know.

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:19.901
And they are the kinds of
people that, for me,

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:22.601
I was like, "I'm, one, going to
know them the rest of my life,

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:26.434
and, two, anytime they call,
I've got to be there."

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:29.000
So if they're like, "Hey, Mi,
why don't you come in

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.734
and do a small bit on a show
we're working on..."

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:32.934
"Great."

00:04:32.934 --> 00:04:35.801
"Hey, if you could take us
to the airport..."

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:37.734
"Sure."

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:40.634
-That's why you're here.
You're there for each other.

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:41.801
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:44.567
-They know how
to write, too, huh?

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:46.434
-My God, I mean,
it's one of those things

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:50.167
where you don't really think
about the script

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:52.501
because you just trust and
you know it's going to be great.

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:53.901
It's going to be golden.

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:56.667
And, also, I mean, back in the
days of "Gilmore," I mean,

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.667
we had these
massive, massive scripts,

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:00.734
and that, for me,
felt like a proving ground

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:03.801
as an actor to really
soak in the words,

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:05.601
really understand
the poetry of it,

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:07.067
and then deliver it,

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:09.934
you know, put what I can on it
to make it come out naturally,

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:13.567
because, you know, the way
they write is definitely prose.

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:14.834
It's incredible.

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:16.667
-I want to talk about
"This Is Us."

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:18.801
This is the sixth --
This is the final season.

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:20.767
Premiered tonight.
-Yes, it is.

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:23.701
-And you're filming
the final season now.

00:05:23.701 --> 00:05:25.901
And, of course,
everyone's going to ask you,

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:29.367
and I probably know the answer,
but do you know how it ends

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:30.634
or do you know --
or are there still secrets

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:31.767
that you don't know?

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:33.534
Because the show is
always twists and turns,

00:05:33.534 --> 00:05:35.934
and right before it's the --
Two minutes before

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:37.567
the end of the show you're like,
"Oh, I get this."

00:05:37.567 --> 00:05:39.667
And then you're like, "What?!"

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:41.868
-Yeah, yeah. That's how it goes.
-And you're crying.

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:43.467
-I mean, listen, Fogelman --

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:46.868
Dan Fogelman is
incredibly candid with us

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:51.801
about his intentions with
the show, with the characters.

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:56.167
So he kind of ran us through
what he was doing at the end.

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:59.100
So I think I have a
pretty good idea

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.067
of what's going to happen,
what's to come.

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:05.267
But, also -- So, right now,
myself, Mandy, and Justin

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:07.133
are all directing a trilogy.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.534
And we were all on set
right before the break,

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:13.634
and Dan was around and he was
talking about his work

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:15.133
on the last two episodes.

00:06:15.133 --> 00:06:17.334
And, you know,
your heart rate starts going

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:19.534
and the excitement to know
what he's working on.

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:21.033
It's like, "Oh,
this is going to be great."

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:23.801
It's going to absolutely
probably crush people

00:06:23.801 --> 00:06:25.968
in the best possible way,
because that's Fogelman's goal

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:29.033
is to make people feel
something in life.

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:32.133
-Yeah, you start
rolling up your shorts.

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.567
-Yeah,
I start rolling up my shorts.

00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:35.934
-Rolling up the shorts, getting
ready for the thing, yeah.

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:37.501
-I'm ready. Yeah, yeah.
Call Jimmy.

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:40.200
I've got to interview
and do some legs.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:44.400
-I got to see the first episode,
and you're phenomenal in it.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.767
And I want to show a clip here.

00:06:45.767 --> 00:06:47.167
But I thought it was charming,

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:51.400
because it's you
singing to Mandy Moore.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.767
And I just think --
I just know you a little bit,

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:56.400
but I know you, and that's got
to be pressure singing

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.367
to Mandy Moore,
who's a professional singer.

00:06:59.367 --> 00:07:01.501
-Yes. A professional singer

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.434
whose husband is
a professional musician.

00:07:03.434 --> 00:07:06.801
-That's correct, yeah.
-And I have no pipes at all.

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:08.701
I'm not musically inclined.

00:07:08.701 --> 00:07:12.767
But, yet, they are like, "Hey,
we wrote this really sweet scene

00:07:12.767 --> 00:07:16.567
where you're singing
REO Speedwagon to your TV wife."

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:18.367
And I'm like, "Great.
Here we go."

00:07:18.367 --> 00:07:19.868
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-That's love.

00:07:19.868 --> 00:07:21.300
-That is love.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.601
But you were saying something
when you were on the show before

00:07:23.601 --> 00:07:25.601
that when you started working
with Mandy, you kind of made,

00:07:25.601 --> 00:07:27.400
like, a pact with each other.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:28.634
You just said, "Hey..."

00:07:28.634 --> 00:07:31.667
-Yeah. We did. We did.

00:07:31.667 --> 00:07:32.934
Right before the show premiered,

00:07:32.934 --> 00:07:34.400
we were in New York
for the up-fronts,

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.968
the big advertiser conference,

00:07:36.968 --> 00:07:40.133
and everybody
was kind of milling about.

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:42.467
Mandy and I were just, like,
off to the side by ourselves,

00:07:42.467 --> 00:07:45.501
and we just kind of raised
our glasses to one another.

00:07:45.501 --> 00:07:49.067
We almost took vows with
one another, where it was like,

00:07:49.067 --> 00:07:51.334
"Hey, I promise
to always communicate.

00:07:51.334 --> 00:07:54.934
I promise to not be happy
until you're happy.

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:56.734
I will always look out for you."
And all that.

00:07:56.734 --> 00:08:00.767
And we have stayed very true to
what we said in the beginning.

00:08:00.767 --> 00:08:04.133
I mean, I've got to say,
she has been probably,

00:08:04.133 --> 00:08:06.467
in my 26 years
in front of the camera,

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:08.601
the best partner I've ever had.

00:08:08.601 --> 00:08:13.267
Her commitment, her dedication,
her growth as an artist.

00:08:13.267 --> 00:08:15.000
Like, you know, the audience --

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.501
you guys all get to watch
the show in its entirety.

00:08:18.501 --> 00:08:21.801
I get to sit there in front of
her or stand in front of her

00:08:21.801 --> 00:08:25.334
or lay in a bed next to her
and watch, front row,

00:08:25.334 --> 00:08:28.734
what she does
and how impactful it is,

00:08:28.734 --> 00:08:31.767
the work is to her,
and I've only seen it grow.

00:08:31.767 --> 00:08:37.067
So it's been a pleasure to be
her TV husband for six years,

00:08:37.067 --> 00:08:38.400
and, at the same time,

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:41.000
closing this chapter,
I'm very excited to see

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.000
what Mandy does next,
because she's such a force.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.434
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:45.434 --> 00:08:48.534
Here's Milo Ventimiglia in the
new season of "This Is Us."

00:08:48.534 --> 00:08:49.601
Take a look at this.

00:08:49.601 --> 00:08:52.234
-REO Speedwagon are
the new Beatles.

00:08:52.234 --> 00:08:54.067
You remember I said that.
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:54.067 --> 00:09:00.300
-♪ What started out as
friendship has grown stronger ♪

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.234
♪ I only wish I had
the strength to let it show ♪

00:09:04.234 --> 00:09:06.367
-Oh, you're letting it show.
-I am?

00:09:06.367 --> 00:09:07.367
-Mm-hmm.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:12.667
-Okay, break it up, people.

00:09:12.667 --> 00:09:14.200
-Big day.
-Big day.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:15.734
-I know. Hey, guys.

00:09:15.734 --> 00:09:18.234
See what I have for you
in honor of today?

00:09:18.234 --> 00:09:19.601
Tang.

00:09:19.601 --> 00:09:21.133
-Tang!
-Hold on, hold on, hold on.

00:09:21.133 --> 00:09:22.734
-Whoa! Slow down. Slow down.

00:09:22.734 --> 00:09:27.501
Okay, now, dad's off.
So goodbye kiss, kiss, kiss.

00:09:27.501 --> 00:09:29.534
I want all the details later.

00:09:29.534 --> 00:09:31.501
Um...briefcase?

00:09:31.501 --> 00:09:32.734
-In the living room.

00:09:32.734 --> 00:09:34.200
-What would I do without you?

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:37.267
-Yeah. REO Speedwagon.
-What would I do with her?

00:09:37.267 --> 00:09:40.300
-REO Speedwagon
is the new Beatles.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.534
-Yeah!
-Milo Ventimiglia, everybody.

00:09:41.534 --> 00:09:45.801
"This Is Us" airs Tuesdays
at 9:00 p.m. on NBC.

